<title>USA: Venezuela says it cleared arrears with Paris Club.</title>
<headline>Venezuela says it cleared arrears with Paris Club.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela has paid $58 million to clear arrears on its Paris Club debt, Venezuelan Finance Minister Luis Raul Matos Azocar said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Venezuela's all paid up with the Paris Club,&quot; Matos told reporters after attending a business conference on the fringes of the International Monetary Fund/World Bank spring meeting.</p>
<p>The Venezuelan government paid $35 million to Spain and $23 million to France, he added.</p>
<p>((-- Washington newsroom +1 202 898 8489))</p>
</text>
